# adapters/pytest.sh — gate_e2e rewritten from Playwright to pytest markers.
# A Home Assistant custom component has no deployable HTTP artifact, so the e2e tier is
# `pytest -m "e2e and m<n>"`. Upstream's version returns PENDING forever here, which would make
# every milestone unlandable. UPSTREAM CANDIDATE: teach the stock pytest adapter to fall back to a
# pytest-marker e2e tier when e2e/playwright.config.ts is absent, and this entry can be deleted.
adapters/pytest.sh

# Same file, second local fix: gate_build. Stock version (a) ran `compileall -q src` in a repo whose
# sources are in custom_components/ (compileall exits 0 on a missing dir, so the miss was silent) and
# (b) used `python3 -m ruff check .`, whose module entry point EXITS 0 while printing "Found N
# errors" — only the `ruff` executable propagates the status. Together they made gate_build incapable
# of failing. Proven by injecting an unused import: PASS before, FAIL after. UPSTREAM CANDIDATE.

